      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This report documents how intravascular ultrasound imaging was used to diagnose a short \"napkin-ring\" stenosis that was missed by coronary angiography. Intravascular ultrasound revealed a lumen of 2.6 x 2.5 mm in diameter and 5.0 mm2 in cross-sectional area, with a residual atheroma that occluded 63% of available cross-sectional area at the stenosis."},
